{"type":"assistant","uuid":"00408561-37c4-4431-a6ee-87afe944e162","session_id":"44e59bfe-2b0d-416c-9095-bdb1e6e3a70d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"00408561-37c4-4431-a6ee-87afe944e162","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the complete fix:\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root Cause:** The `Util.getPreferences()` method used a hardcoded preference filename (`\"org.moire.ultrasonic_preferences\"`) instead of the app's actual default preferences file. In debug builds, the app ID is `org.moire.ultrasonic.debug` (due to `applicationIdSuffix \".debug\"`), so `PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences()` creates a different file (`org.moire.ultrasonic.debug_preferences`). When `ServerSettingsFragment` saves server credentials using `getDefaultSharedPreferences()` and `MusicServiceFactory` reads them using the hardcoded filename, they access different files — credentials appear null, and the fallback to `http://localhost` is triggered.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `Util.getPreferences()` to use `PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences(context)` instead of the hardcoded filename, making it consistent with the rest of the codebase (`ServerSettingsFragment`, `SettingsFragment`, `getActiveServers()`).\n\n---\n\n## Patch\n\n```diff\n--- a/ultrasonic/src/main/java/org/moire/ultrasonic/util/Util.java\n+++ b/ultrasonic/src/main/java/org/moire/ultrasonic/util/Util.java\n@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@ public class Util extends DownloadActivity\n \n \tpublic static SharedPreferences getPreferences(Context context)\n \t{\n-\t\treturn context.getSharedPreferences(Constants.PREFERENCES_FILE_NAME, 0);\n+\t\treturn PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences(context);\n \t}\n \n \tpublic static int getRemainingTrialDays(Context context)\n```\n\n**File modified:** `ultrasonic/src/main/java/org/moire/ultrasonic/util/Util.java` (line 403)\n\n**Why this works:** `PreferenceManager.getDefaultSharedPreferences(context)` uses the application context to derive the correct preference file name from the actual `applicationId` (including any `.debug` suffix for debug builds), ensuring `getPreferences()` returns the same `SharedPreferences` instance that `ServerSettingsFragment` writes to."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55421,"output_tokens":461,"cache_read_input_tokens":54912,"total_tokens":55882}}}
